## Implementation Pattern
```rust
fn kill_selected_worker(&mut self) {
    // Check if connected to server
    if self.server_client_tx.is_some() {
        // Get selected worker ID
        let worker_id = self.get_selected_worker_id(); // Need to extract this
        if let Some(id) = worker_id {
            self.send_server_client_request(ServerClientRequest::KillWorker { 
                worker_id: id 
            });
            self.status_message = Some(format!("Requested to kill worker {}", id));
        }
        return;
    }

    // Existing direct kill logic...
}
```

## Notes
- The function currently shows a dialog then calls `kill_worker_by_id`
- Need to extract the worker_id from the selected worker before the client mode check
- The worker_id is used in the server request, not the local session name
